{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["He gave the people favor — to give to them as a gift, as it is written in Exodus: ונתן את חן העם בעיני מצרים." "And they asked of them — Egyptian to Israelite: Israel were the borrowers and Egyptians the lenders. They completed their request, and it was a gift. The one who requests a thing is called the pōʿel, and the one who hands over what is requested is called the mapʿil. The mashʾil gives him what he requests." "And they stripped Egypt — their ornaments: they asked for and put them on their sons and on their daughters, as it is written: ויתנצלו בני ישראל את עדים מהר חורב."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:18.601355429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}